## Summary

Implemented PRD-076 (Scope Modularization for Parallel Authoring) in full. All six acceptance criteria are met.

**Changed/added files** (50 total):
- **Config split**: `crates/familiar-ai-core/src/config.rs` (5164 lines) → `config/` tree of 21 per-feature files (providers, registry, review, delivery, driver, accounting, compression, inference, daemon, watcher, tray, summary, rollup, packer, dashboard, artifacts, worker, repository, preflight, shareable_toml, mod.rs), all re-exported at the same paths. Behavior preservation proven by a pinned SHA-256 hash test of `Config::default()`'s serialization, computed against the pre-refactor code and asserted unchanged post-refactor.
- **CLI thinning**: `bin/familiar-ai.rs` (2563 → 540 lines) now holds only arg-parsing types and dispatch; subcommand logic moved into 9 new `crates/familiar-ai-daemon/src/cli/*.rs` modules. Resolved a module-name collision by renaming the daemon's own unrelated `src/cli.rs` to `daemon_cli.rs`.
- **Contracts split**: `docs/contracts/providers.md` → `providers-index.md` + 5 domain docs (inference, credentials, billing, deploy, registry), existing text preserved verbatim.
- **PRD amendments**: narrowed `expected_files` in 038, 053, 058, 059, 060, 061, 063, 071, 072, 073 (structured) and 032 (legacy) to point at the new per-feature files instead of the four shared surfaces.
- **Execution plan**: `EXECUTION-PLAN.md` regenerated with real numbers from the scheduler's own `achievable_width` function (verified via a temporary probe, then reverted) — wave 5 = achievable width 2 (was serializing at 1), wave 6 = 2, wave 7 = 2 (fully disjoint). PRD-076 itself marked completed and moved to `docs/prds/done/`.

**Verification**: full workspace build and test suite green (workspace `--no-default-features` for the daemon crate, since this sandbox lacks `libxdo`/tray system libs — confirmed pre-existing by reproducing the same link failure on unmodified code); `cargo fmt --check` clean; `cargo clippy` clean except one pre-existing `bootstrap.rs` lint and one pre-existing `summary_worker.rs` dead-code warning, both confirmed untouched and reproducing identically before this change; `familiar-ai backlog metadata-check --advisory` exits 0 with zero structured-v1 diagnostics; `prd_fixtures.rs` pins unaffected.

One operational note: the two subagents doing the config split and CLI split ran concurrently in the same shared worktree and briefly interfered with each other's git state (stash cycles). I verified the final combined result compiles and tests pass, and dropped the now-redundant leftover stash entries.
